      "subtitle": "What is WARDOGS? It is a 100-player three-squad tactical FPS developed by BULKHEAD and published by Team17 on Steam under AppID 1867240. It entered Steam Early Access on September 10, 2026 at $39.99 USD with a $54.99 Supporter Edition, after a Closed Beta weekend that ran 2026-08-21 to 2026-08-23. The mode is a 2x2km three-squad Control Zone race to 100 points, supported by a persistent cash economy and a gold bars / Black Market / Vault end-game.\n\n## What is WARDOGS in genre terms\n\nWARDOGS sits inside the tactical military shooter genre with an extraction-adjacent cash loop bolted on. Three squads of up to 100 players total fight over a single 2x2km Control Zone, and the first squad to 100 points on a 30-second scoring tick wins the round. The mode lineage is ARMA KOTH, a king-of-the-hill pattern lifted into a three-faction economy. Genre tags on Steam include Action, FPS, Tactical, Shooter, War and Multiplayer.\n\nThe cash loop is the part that pushes the game past a traditional tactical shooter. Each squad starts a Control Zone round with $10,000 in match cash, and that cash carries between matches rather than resetting. At season end, persistent cash converts into gold bars, which feed a Black Market and a Vault end-game. That combination \u2014 three-faction king-of-the-hill plus persistent cash plus gold bar end-game \u2014 is the identity a launch-window search user should anchor on.\n\n## Who made WARDOGS and how it launched\n\nThe developer is BULKHEAD, a UK-based studio. WARDOGS is a new IP for the studio and not a sequel, port or remake \u2014 the Steam AppID 1867240 is a fresh listing on 2026-09-28. The publisher is Team17, which has shipped other indie and AA titles through Steam and is listed as the publisher credit on the store page. The BULKHEAD website and FAQ and the Team17 publisher site are both identity-confirmation only.\n\nThe launch is a Steam-only Early Access event. The EA window opened on September 10, 2026, with a $39.99 USD base price and a $54.99 USD Supporter Edition. Eurogamer's pre-launch coverage confirms there is no micro-transaction beyond the two editions, and Games.gg confirms the Steam wishlist signal is approaching nearly one million. The Closed Beta weekend (2026-08-21 to 2026-08-23) is the only public pre-launch test and is already past as of the 2026-09-28 research date.\n\n## Mode and gameplay loop at a glance\n\nThe headline mode is Control Zone. Three squads spawn into a random 2x2km area and race for control points on a 30-second scoring tick. The first squad to 100 points wins. A Hot Zone doubles the cash reward inside the active control area, which pushes squads into contested fights rather than passive holds. The loop is supported by destructible and buildable environments: rocket launchers can collapse apartment buildings, tanks can shove through towns, Fortify calls lock down strongpoints, and forward operating bases give squads a respawn anchor.\n\nInside the squad, deployable roles layer the loop. The named roles on the Steam page and the BULKHD 'Early Access & Beyond' reveal include a ghillie suit sniper for long-range overwatch, an arms dealer who sells to squadmates, a supply-ferry helicopter pilot, an artillery role that locks down an area, a builder who Fortifies locations and a medic who keeps the squad alive. Fighter jets are framed as a later-season unlockable. Each role interacts with the cash economy \u2014 roles are purchased with match cash rather than unlocked on a fixed progression tree.\n\n## Why the launch identity matters\n\nWARDOGS is positioned as a 100-player three-squad tactical FPS with a persistent cash economy. That positioning is the load-bearing identity for the launch window \u2014 it tells a search user what mode they will be playing, how long a round takes, and how the cash loop fits. Easy Anti-Cheat Kernel Level on the Steam page covers the anti-cheat surface, and the 14 supported UI languages (including Simplified Chinese) cover the localisation surface at EA. Specific weapon and vehicle pricing, gold bar exchange rates and post-EA roadmap items are subject to Early Access tuning on 2026-09-28.\n\nThe launch is single-store and single-platform on day one. Windows PC via Steam is the only confirmed platform on 2026-09-28, and PS5, Xbox Series X|S, Switch, Switch 2 and Steam Deck verified status are not announced. The Steam store page for AppID 1867240 is the canonical fact source, and the BULKHD 'Early Access & Beyond' reveal is the canonical gameplay source for the launch window.",
