    "quickAnswer": "WARDOGS closed beta ran the weekend of August 21-23, 2026, ahead of the Steam Early Access launch on September 10. Pre-order customers and a small invited test group got access, with the Steam store page noting Easy Anti-Cheat Kernel Level for cheater-free testing. The Closed Beta is distinct from earlier Closed Test alpha phases. Future playtest registrations and additional test weekends are not announced as of 2026-09-28.\n\n## WARDOGS closed beta dates and what ran\n\nThe WARDOGS closed beta was scheduled for August 21-23, 2026, with the weekend acting as the final pre-launch shake-down before the September 10 Early Access launch on Steam (AppID 1867240). Both the Steam store page and Eurogamer's pre-launch coverage confirm the same three-day window. Easy Anti-Cheat Kernel Level was active during the weekend, which BULKHEAD framed as a cheater-free testing condition so that balance, server load and Control Zone pacing could be evaluated against live traffic rather than internal QA only.\n\nThe Closed Beta was positioned as a stress and tuning event, not a public open weekend. That distinction matters because players who search for \"WARDOGS beta\" sometimes assume the event is still upcoming; on 2026-09-28 it has already concluded. Anyone searching today for a WARDOGS closed beta sign-up link is too late for this specific round.\n\n## Who got into the WARDOGS closed beta\n\nAccess was limited to two groups. First, customers who pre-ordered WARDOGS through Steam before the August 21 cut-off received automatic access to the beta client. Second, a smaller invited test group selected from prior Closed Test sign-ups, Discord interest channels and Steam Playtest Request entries also got in. BULKHEAD did not publish a public queue or first-come-first-served form, so the only practical way to secure a slot was either a Steam pre-order or an invite.\n\nThe closed beta access model also meant that no public Steam Playtest Request signup is open today. Insider Gaming and Eurogamer both reported the closed beta as invite-and-pre-order only on the same 2026-08-21 window. The Steam store page now shows the Early Access launch (September 10) as the next playable milestone, not a follow-up beta.\n\n## How the Closed Beta differs from the earlier Closed Test\n\nWARDOGS ran a series of earlier Closed Test alpha phases in 2025 and 2026, primarily through Discord interest channels and Steam Playtest Request. Those rounds focused on core Control Zone mechanics and balance pacing, and were smaller and more frequent than the August 2026 closed beta. The August 21-23 weekend was the last pre-EA stress test, with a wider pre-order audience and Easy Anti-Cheat Kernel Level enforcement.\n\nIf you are searching for \"WARDOGS beta\" or \"WARDOGS closed beta\" on 2026-09-28, the relevant event is the August 21-23 weekend, which has already ended. Earlier alpha phases are not currently accepting new sign-ups. Future public test weekends are not announced as of 2026-09-28.",
