        "body": "## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n### What are the WARDOGS Steam genres?\n\nThe Steam store page for WARDOGS lists five store-defined genres: Action, FPS, Tactical, Shooter and War. The genre block is editorial and stable across regional storefronts.\n\n### What are the WARDOGS user tags?\n\nThe user tags currently surfaced on the WARDOGS Steam page include Multiplayer, Team-Based, Military, Action, Strategy, Shooter, First-Person, Tactical and War. User tags are applied by Steam shoppers and can shift as wishlists convert to ownership and reviews come in.\n\n### Is WARDOGS tagged as a battle royale or hero shooter?\n\nNo. The WARDOGS tags do not include battle royale or hero shooter. The combination of Tactical, Team-Based, Strategy, Military and First-Person tags points to a 100-player three-squad tactical shooter with persistent economy rather than a shrinking-zone or hero-ability model.\n\n### Why does WARDOGS show up under Tactical searches?\n\nThe Tactical label appears in both the editorial genre block and the user-tag list, and the Strategy user tag reinforces it. Together these tags, plus the Team-Based and First-Person tags, are why the page surfaces under tactical-shooter search results on Steam.\n\n### Do WARDOGS tags change during Early Access?\n\nThe editorial genre block is stable. The user-tag list is community-applied and can shift as more players own and review the game. As of 2026-09-28, BULKHEAD has not announced any post-EA tag change, but the community user-tag surface should be re-checked if you are searching months later."
