        "id": "faq",
        "type": "prose",
        "heading": "Frequently asked questions",
        "body": "## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n### What is the core WARDOGS gameplay loop?\n\nThe core loop is: deploy into a Control Zone as one of three squads, earn cash through kills and objective ticks, race to 100 points, then carry cash and equipment into the next match. Roles, vehicles and Hot Zone bonuses all feed into that four-beat loop.\n\n### How many players are in a WARDOGS match?\n\nA standard WARDOGS match holds 100 players split across three squads of roughly 33 players each. That 100-player three-squad structure is consistent across the Control Zone mode and the Hardcore variant.\n\n### How does persistent cash work in WARDOGS gameplay?\n\nCash earned in one match carries over to the next, after subtracting what you spend on deployable roles, vehicles and equipment. End-of-season gold bars act as a separate end-game currency earned through the cash economy rather than direct cash itself.\n\n### What deployable roles are available at launch?\n\nConfirmed launch roles include ghillie suit sniper, arms dealer, supply-ferry helicopter pilot, artillery, builder and medic. Unlockable fighter jets are referenced by BULKHD as a later-season addition rather than a launch role.\n\n### Does WARDOGS have destructible environments?\n\nYes. Rocket launchers, tanks and Fortify are all confirmed environmental tools that can take down or reinforce buildings, town blocks and forward operating bases inside the 2x2km Control Zone. Destructibility is part of the standard WARDOGS gameplay rather than a separate mode.\n\n### Does WARDOGS have a Hardcore mode?\n\nYes. Hardcore mode removes killcam, simplifies the HUD, limits the kill feed to the player's own squad and forces vehicles into first-person camera. It applies to the same Control Zone map pool and the same cash economy."
