        "type": "prose",
        "heading": "Frequently asked questions",
        "body": "## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n### How big is the WARDOGS Control Zone?\n\nEach Control Zone round plays out inside a 2x2km random sub-zone of the larger map. The 2x2km footprint is the same on every launch map, but the sub-zone position varies round to round.\n\n### How many players are in a WARDOGS Control Zone match?\n\nA standard match holds 100 players split across three squads of roughly 33 players each. The three-squad split is what differentiates the mode from a traditional two-team King-of-the-Hill round.\n\n### How does scoring work in WARDOGS Control Zone?\n\nThe squad holding the Control Zone gains points on a 30-second tick. The first squad to reach 100 points wins the round. Squads that lose the zone keep the points already banked.\n\n### What is a Hot Zone in WARDOGS Control Zone?\n\nA Hot Zone is a smaller sub-area inside the 2x2km box that pays out double cash when scoring ticks fire while a squad holds it. It is the high-leverage cash objective within the wider zone.\n\n### How is WARDOGS Control Zone different from ARMA KOTH?\n\nWARDOGS Control Zone scales to 100 players across three squads, adds a persistent cash economy that carries across deployments and layers a Hot Zone bonus on top of the main 30-second ticks. Traditional ARMA KOTH is two-team, single-zone and has no persistent cash carry.\n\n### Does WARDOGS Control Zone have destructible environments?\n\nYes. The 2x2km sub-zone plays on the same launch maps with destructible buildings, buildable Fortify positions and forward operating bases. Destructibility is part of the standard Control Zone ruleset rather than a separate variant."
