        "id": "faq",
        "type": "prose",
        "heading": "Frequently asked questions",
        "body": "## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n### What is the starting cash in a WARDOGS match?\n\nWARDOGS economy gives every operator a $10,000 wallet at the start of each Control Zone round, per the Steam store page for AppID 1867240 and BULKHEAD's reveal. Unspent cash carries into the next round.\n\n### Do you keep cash across deaths in WARDOGS?\n\nYes. The WARDOGS economy is persistent across deaths and across matches, so cash earned during a round stays in the wallet on respawn and into the next drop. Specific respawn cash penalties are subject to Early Access tuning as of 2026-09-28.\n\n### What are gold bars used for in WARDOGS?\n\nGold bars are the end-of-season end-game currency in the WARDOGS economy. They feed the Black Market vendor for high-tier items and the Vault system for long-term savings, both confirmed by the Steam store description.\n\n### Is there a microtransaction store in WARDOGS?\n\nEurogamer's pre-launch coverage states there is no microtransaction in WARDOGS at EA launch. Beyond the $39.99 EA and $54.99 Supporter Edition listed on Steam, the cash and gold bars economy is the only confirmed way to unlock items as of 2026-09-28.\n\n### Does Hardcore mode change the WARDOGS economy?\n\nHardcore mode removes killcam, simplifies the HUD, limits kill feed to squad, and forces vehicles into first-person. Whether Hardcore mode changes the cash wallet or gold bar exchange is not announced as of 2026-09-28."
