        "id": "faq",
        "type": "prose",
        "heading": "Frequently asked questions",
        "body": "## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n### What classes are in WARDOGS at launch?\n\nWARDOGS roles at Steam Early Access launch are the ghillie suit sniper, arms dealer, supply-ferry helicopter, artillery piece, builder kit, and medic, per the Steam store page for AppID 1867240 and BULKHEAD's \"Early Access & Beyond\" reveal.\n\n### Are fighter jets in WARDOGS at launch?\n\nFighter jets are confirmed as a future unlockable WARDOGS role that will arrive later in the EA cycle. The exact season for the fighter jet unlock is not announced as of 2026-09-28.\n\n### Do WARDOGS roles change between squads?\n\nYes. WARDOGS roles are bought with the per-match cash wallet and carry across deaths, so each squad picks its own mix. A squad's role mix is the main way it differentiates itself inside the 100-player three-squad Control Zone race.\n\n### What does the arms dealer role do?\n\nThe arms dealer role sells ammunition, attachments, and consumables to teammates inside the squad. It is the most direct bridge between the WARDOGS cash economy and the rest of the squad.\n\n### Is the builder role good for holding Control Zone?\n\nThe builder role deploys Fortify placements on key locations and forward operating bases, which is the same destructible-and-buildable framing the Steam store description highlights. It is the strongest role for turning a contested point into a held point."
