        "body": "## Frequently Asked Questions\n\n### Where can I watch the official WARDOGS trailer?\n\nThe official WARDOGS trailer lives on the Steam store page for AppID 1867240, surfaced as the page's primary trailer frame on 2026-09-28, and on BULKHEAD's official YouTube channel as the \"Early Access & Beyond\" reveal video (published 2026-04-07). Both are current-game footage and both are the canonical trailer source for the launch window.\n\n### Is the BULKHEAD \"Early Access & Beyond\" video the same as the Steam trailer?\n\nThey cover overlapping WARDOGS footage but are different cuts. The BULKHD \"Early Access & Beyond\" reveal is the announcement-stage deep cut that walks through mode, economy and roles; the Steam store trailer frame is the launch-window trailer anchored on the September 10, 2026 EA date. Search users wanting the EA launch trailer should anchor on the Steam frame; search users wanting the announcement-stage reveal should anchor on the BULKHD YouTube reveal.\n\n### How do I avoid the 2016 \"War Dogs\" movie trailer when searching for the WARDOGS trailer?\n\nAnchor on the Steam store page for AppID 1867240 or the BULKHEAD YouTube channel \u2014 both are clearly labelled with the BULKHD developer credit and the Team17 publisher credit, and neither is the 2016 Todd Phillips film starring Jonah Hill and Miles Teller. The film trailer is unrelated and is presented as discovery-only noise on this page.\n\n### Does WARDOGS have a launch cinematic or alternate language trailer?\n\nA launch cinematic, dubbed language variants or alternate cuts are not announced as of 2026-09-28. The Steam store page and the BULKHD \"Early Access & Beyond\" reveal are the only published current-game trailer sources at the research date. Any future cinematic or language-specific trailer would surface on the Steam store page and on BULKHD's official YouTube channel first.\n\n### Is there a separate gameplay trailer for the WARDOGS Control Zone mode?\n\nThe \"Early Access & Beyond\" reveal on BULKHD's YouTube channel carries the gameplay framing for Control Zone, the persistent cash economy, the deployable roles and the vehicles. There is no separate, dedicated Control Zone gameplay trailer on the Steam store page as of 2026-09-28; the BULKHD YouTube reveal is the canonical gameplay-side trailer.\n\n### Will the WARDOGS trailer change after Early Access launch?\n\nPost-launch trailer updates, season trailer updates, or a separate EA cinematic are not announced as of 2026-09-28. Any future trailer update would be reflected on the Steam store page for AppID 1867240 and on BULKHD's official YouTube channel first. Treat those two surfaces as the canonical trailer check on every re-read."
