      "subtitle": "WARDOGS reviews on the Steam Early Access store page are not yet aggregated into a public band as of the 2026-09-28 research date. The Steam review band only fills in once enough player reviews come in after EA launch on September 10, 2026. The pre-launch reception signal is the wishlist total near one million per Games.gg plus the August 21-23, 2026 Closed Beta weekend covered by Eurogamer. Third-party outlet review scores are not announced as of 2026-09-28.\n\n## WARDOGS reviews: launch window status as of 2026-09-28\n\nWARDOGS reviews in the launch window are a dated-status answer, not a numeric band. The Steam Early Access launch landed on September 10, 2026, and the public Steam review band needs enough written reviews from paying players before it (and any Steam Curator aggregate) settles. As of the 2026-09-28 research date, that band is not yet aggregated into a published number on the Steam store page for AppID 1867240. Search users landing on this page expecting a percentage or a \"Mostly Positive\" label will get that label once the post-EA review sample size is large enough to publish, not on the day EA goes live.\n\nThe same launch-window situation applies to third-party outlets (Polygon, Eurogamer, IGN, PC Gamer, etc.). Pre-launch coverage from Eurogamer exists and is the most-cited outlet piece covering the closed beta window, EA pricing and the wishlist signal, but a scored review from those outlets has not been published as of 2026-09-28. Numeric WARDOGS review scores from major outlets should be treated as not announced as of 2026-09-28 unless re-confirmed directly through that outlet's review URL.\n\n## Pre-launch wishlist signal and Closed Beta reception\n\nThe pre-launch reception signal for WARDOGS sits on two surfaces. First, the Steam wishlist count approaches nearly one million per Games.gg, confirmed on 2026-09-28. Second, the Closed Beta weekend (2026-08-21 to 2026-08-23) gave paying pre-order customers and a smaller invited test group a final pre-launch window under Easy Anti-Cheat Kernel Level, with Eurogamer covering the test and the EA pricing context. The wishlist number is not the same as a review score, but for a brand-new IP it is the strongest public pre-launch reception signal before the EA review band fills in.\n\nThe Closed Beta reception narrative from Eurogamer centers on the EA launch framing rather than a graded review \u2014 the play session validated the 2x2km three-squad Control Zone pacing, the persistent cash economy and the deployable role surface, without BULKHEAD publishing a beta-to-launch change log. Search users today who want a \"WARDOGS review\" should anchor on the wishlist total plus the Closed Beta coverage, and re-check this page once the public Steam review band is published.\n\n## What changes after EA review band fills in\n\nOnce enough player reviews come in after EA launch on September 10, 2026, the Steam store page for AppID 1867240 will show a public Steam review band. When that band appears, this page's release-window status framing can be replaced with the published Steam review count and band label, sourced from the store page. The same update path covers third-party outlet reviews that publish after EA \u2014 both surface through the Steam store page and the outlet's review URL.\n\nUntil those re-checks happen, the canonical WARDOGS reviews anchor on 2026-09-28 stays at the wishlist total, the Closed Beta weekend coverage, and the dated \"EA Steam review band is not yet aggregated\" framing above. Search users arriving through IGN, Reddit or YouTube should re-check the Steam store page before quoting a WARDOGS review number.",
